    "question": "Ellen’s doctor instructed her to eat a 2,200 calorie a day diet. For breakfast, she ate 353 calories. For lunch, she had 885. She had an afternoon snack of 130 calories. How many calories does she have left for dinner?",
    "gold": "832",
    "answer": "Ellen ate 353 calories for breakfast + 885 for lunch + 130 for a snack = <<353+885+130=1368>>1368 calories.\nEllen has 2,200 calories – 1368 = <<2200-1368=832>>832 calories left for dinner.\n#### 832"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many calories Ellen has left for dinner, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of calories Ellen has consumed so far.\n2. Subtract the total calories consumed from her daily calorie limit.\n\nFirst, let's find the total number of calories Ellen has consumed for breakfast, lunch, and her afternoon snack:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total calories consumed} = \\text{Calories for breakfast} + \\text{Calories for lunch} + \\text{Calories for snack}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total calories consumed} = 353 + 885 + 130\n\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\n\\[\n353 + 885 = 1238\n\\]\n\\[\n1238 + 130 = 1368\n\\]\n\nSo, Ellen has consumed 1368 calories so far.\n\nNext, we subtract the total calories consumed from her daily calorie limit to find out how many calories she has left for dinner:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Calories left for dinner} = \\text{Daily calorie limit} - \\text{Total calories consumed}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Calories left for dinner} = 2200 - 1368\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these values:\n\n\\[\n2200 - 1368 = 832\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Ellen has \\boxed{832} calories left for dinner.",
